# Architecture

Use a provider-adapter architecture.

Do NOT couple application logic directly to one availability API.

Conceptually:

```text
                        ┌──────────────────────┐
                        │     React client     │
                        └──────────┬───────────┘
                                   │
                      generate/search request
                                   │
                         ┌─────────▼─────────┐
                         │ Cloudflare Worker │
                         └─────────┬─────────┘
                                   │
             ┌─────────────────────┴─────────────────────┐
             │                                           │
     ┌───────▼────────┐                         ┌────────▼────────┐
     │ Naming engine  │                         │ Search/session  │
     │                │                         │ orchestration   │
     └───────┬────────┘                         └────────┬────────┘
             │                                           │
       seed concepts                              candidate batches
             │                                           │
     ┌───────▼────────┐                         ┌────────▼────────┐
     │ deterministic  │                         │ availability    │
     │ expansion      │                         │ provider layer  │
     └───────┬────────┘                         └────────┬────────┘
             │                                           │
       500-5000 names                   ┌────────────────┼───────────────┐
             │                          │                │               │
             └─────────────────────────►│ Dotsweep      │ NameSilo      │
                                        │ adapter        │ adapter       │
                                        └────────────────┼───────────────┘
                                                         │
                                                optional RDAP fallback
```

Define an interface similar to:

```ts
interface AvailabilityProvider {
  id: string;

  maxBatchSize: number;

  check(
    domains: string[],
    context?: CheckContext
  ): Promise<AvailabilityResult[]>;
}
```

And:

```ts
type AvailabilityStatus =
  | "available"
  | "taken"
  | "unknown"
  | "invalid"
  | "reserved";

type Confidence =
  | "certain"
  | "estimated"
  | "unknown";

interface AvailabilityResult {
  domain: string;
  status: AvailabilityStatus;
  confidence: Confidence;

  provider: string;
  source?: "rdap" | "registrar" | "dns" | "whois" | "cache";

  registrationPrice?: number;
  renewalPrice?: number;
  currency?: string;

  premium?: boolean;

  checkedAt: string;

  error?: string;
}
```

Never turn `unknown` into `available`.

Never turn a timeout into `available`.

Never infer authoritative availability solely from:

* NXDOMAIN;
* no A record;
* no NS record;
* blank WHOIS output;
* HTTP failure.

