# AI naming architecture

This is extremely important.

DO NOT ask the model:

> Generate 1,000 domain names.

That wastes tokens and generally produces repetitive garbage.

Instead use a two-stage system.

## Stage 1 — semantic decomposition

Send one structured request to the language model.

Input:

```json
{
  "description": "...",
  "liked_names": [],
  "disliked_names": [],
  "required_words": [],
  "optional_words": [],
  "extensions": [".com"],
  "max_length": 14,
  "allow_numbers": false,
  "allow_hyphens": false,
  "tone": ["credible", "modern", "memorable"]
}
```

Ask the model to output structured naming material rather than final domains.

Example schema:

```ts
interface NamingAtoms {
  coreConcepts: string[];
  relatedNouns: string[];
  relatedVerbs: string[];
  industryTerms: string[];
  metaphors: string[];
  shortSynonyms: string[];
  prefixes: string[];
  suffixes: string[];
  greekLatinRoots: string[];
  compressedForms: string[];
  phoneticFragments: string[];
  tonalDirections: string[];
  avoid: string[];
}
```

For the AgentWatch example it might discover semantic regions such as:

```text
agent
watch
spy
eye
scope
scan
radar
pulse
signal
wire
beat
brief
report
news
desk
feed
now
track
trace
peek
sentry
beacon
lens
observe
intel
index
map
grid
loop
```

The important thing is semantic diversity.

---

# Stage 2 — deterministic expansion

Create a TypeScript naming engine that expands the atoms into hundreds or thousands of candidates locally without additional LLM calls.

Implement multiple generators.

## A. Direct compounds

```text
agent + pulse
agent + scan
agent + wire
```

## B. Reverse compounds

```text
pulse + agent
watch + agent
```

## C. Prefix constructions

```text
get + signal
try + radar
open + scope
```

Only use these if appropriate.

## D. Suffix constructions

```text
scope + hub
watch + lab
agent + base
```

## E. Portmanteau generation

Create overlap-aware merging.

Examples:

```text
radar + agent
agent + intel
signal + agent
```

Do not merely concatenate everything.

Implement overlap detection:

```text
alpha + halo
-> alphalo
```

Search for suffix-prefix overlaps of 1-4 letters.

## F. Controlled vowel deletion

Optional.

Only permit when resulting name remains obvious and pronounceable.

Bad:

```text
agntwchr
```

Potentially acceptable:

```text
tumblr-style transformations
```

Use sparingly.

## G. Phonetic/invented names

Generate pronounceable constructions based upon permitted phonetic fragments.

Rules:

* 2-4 syllables preferred;
* alternate consonant/vowel groups;
* no impossible consonant clusters;
* avoid names that require explanation to spell;
* no random `x`, `z`, `q` spam.

## H. Semantic metaphor names

Allow domains whose meaning conveys the product without literally containing the keyword.

For agent-news monitoring:

```text
lookout
sentry
beacon
pulse
wire
scope
signal
radar
```

Combine those concepts intelligently.

## I. Numeric variants

Only when enabled by the user.

Support:

```text
11
24
24x7
247
360
365
77
101
```

Numbers should be deliberate rather than random.

