# Availability-first reranking

The key insight is:

The best taken domain is useless.

Therefore availability is part of ranking, not something displayed afterward.

Pipeline:

```text
generate
↓
normalize
↓
cheap deterministic scoring
↓
remove bottom 30-50%
↓
availability check
↓
discard taken
↓
rerank available set
↓
optional AI reranker on top 20-50
```

Do not spend expensive AI evaluation on taken names.

---

# Optional final AI judge

Once availability filtering has reduced 500 names to perhaps 15-70 viable domains, send only those finalists to an LLM.

Ask it to rank them according to:

* memorability;
* semantic fit;
* professional credibility;
* spelling;
* spoken clarity;
* potential ambiguity;
* extensibility;
* avoiding dated startup naming clichés.

Use structured JSON.

The AI judge should never override factual availability.

