# My general "extremely fast products" stack

If you want to develop lots of these products, I'd establish a house architecture.

| Layer                    | Default                                 |
| ------------------------ | --------------------------------------- |
| Static site              | Cloudflare Workers Static Assets        |
| Browser UI               | Preact / lightweight React / vanilla TS |
| Styling                  | CSS                                     |
| Edge gateway             | TypeScript Worker                       |
| Edge routing framework   | none or Hono                            |
| CPU-heavy backend        | Rust + Axum                             |
| Alternative fast backend | Go                                      |
| Streaming human UX       | SSE                                     |
| Streaming agent API      | NDJSON                                  |
| Data format              | JSON initially                          |
| Internal high-volume RPC | Protobuf/gRPC only when justified       |
| Cache                    | edge cache + in-process/cache layer     |
| SQL                      | PostgreSQL                              |
| Global/read-heavy data   | cached materialized data                |
| blobs                    | R2/S3                                   |
| AI                       | behind model abstraction                |
| expensive processing     | queues/jobs                             |
| observability            | OpenTelemetry-compatible tracing        |

Cloudflare itself now recommends Workers Static Assets for new static/full-stack Workers projects rather than the older Workers Sites architecture. ([Cloudflare Docs][7])

